###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# MD cost on a single Intel Xeon Gold core for 64 Si atoms (Table S5): 1.8
# to 4.9 ms per atom per step depending on the model (CHGNet slowest). The
# timed system is not the material of any result, so the timings are held
# in the encoding input. Parameters: M3GNet 664,000, TensorNet 838,000,
# CHGNet 2,700,000.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Introduces MatPES (PBE and r2SCAN); its level of theory and subset sizes are entered in the data-set registry from this paper, and its origin-paper stub is removed.
# - Test MAEs of the MPF, MPtrj and OMat24 models are on the MatPES PBE test set (external to their training data, role external); their training and validation MAEs are on their own data sets.
# - Which MatPES test split the r2SCAN models are evaluated on is read as the r2SCAN split (the text describes only the PBE test set).
# - Magnetic-moment MAEs of the CHGNet models, training-set MAEs, the MatCalc-Benchmark property errors and the MD stability and ionic conductivity benchmarks are not encoded.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: datacite).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kaplan2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

